    description: "**Context.** Measurement `docs/measurements/0032-analysed-repository-as-taint-source.md` (WI-pakag, 2026-11-04). \"The analysed repository never chooses a host_fs path, a subprocess argument or a network destination\" splits in two. The ZONE half shipped as five `repo-content-no-*` claims. The POSITION half — did repo content arrive as the PATH or as the CONTENT of a permitted-zone write, as an ARGV element or as STDIN of a declared launch — is not expressible: no part of the pipeline carries which argument a tainted value reached. The def-use records are `(variable, line)` (`ddg_build`, no `arg_index`), `TaintFlowFinding` records the sink primitive and symbol (`io_boundary.py` ~909: \"The walk carries NO argument identity\"), and the one argument-aware mechanism, the T9 `resource_naming: {names, content, danger}` annotation (WI-bulag), lives on `io_primitives` rows only — the self-catalogue's zone-sink schema admits `module` / `functions` / `methods` / `notes` — and was built for the inverse question (suppress a content flow that merely names a resource) with the soundness guard that a MIXED sink can never be attributed. Measured: a name-in-path fixture and a content-in-content fixture produce byte-identical evidence; on the self tree the permitted-zone flows (user_cache 6, user_out 2, tmp_artifact 1, repo_inspection 117 pairs) had to be adjudicated by reading each sink call (0032 §4), and the three real path/argv rows (`git ls-tree HEAD -- <dir>`, the sanitized route path in a handler-slice filename, hashed git metadata in cache directory names) rest on code facts no claim watches.\n\n**Work.** (1) Each DDG def-use extractor (python, javascript, typescript, go; `LanguageDdgSpec`) records, for a use that is a call argument, the argument index (and keyword name where the language has one). (2) `TaintFlowFinding` gains `sink_arg_index` (None = not attributed), filled by the DDG arm where the chain ends in a call argument; the structural arm leaves it None. (3) Zone-sink rows accept the T9 vocabulary (`resource_naming:` with `names` / `content` / `danger` per function) — extend `_SINK_ENTRY_KEYS` and the loader, reusing `io_boundary`'s parsing — and the ~30 `safety_zones` wrappers are annotated (path-only: `cache_mkdir`, `cache_rmtree`, `cache_unlink`, `user_out_mkdir`, `tmp_artifact_rmtree`, `install_artifact_unlink`, …; mixed: every `*_write*`; argv: `repo_inspect_*`, `backend_index_*`). (4) A claim gains `prohibited_argument_role: resource | content | argv`; the matcher reports a flow against it only when `sink_arg_index` lands in a position the row names for that role, and reports UNATTRIBUTED flows as a caveat, never as clean. (5) Measure on the self tree: the §4 table of 0032 reproduced by the instrument, then the position-half claims added.\n\n**What it is not.** Not a change to the structural arm's reachability semantics; not the T9 suppression rule (which stays as is, soundness guard included).\n\n**Verification.** The two 0032 fixtures read differently (F1 `violated` under `prohibited_argument_role: resource`, F2 not reported but disclosed as a content flow); on the self tree the `_ls_tree_head` row is reported under `argv` and the `cache_write` rows are not; every flow the DDG arm cannot attribute is counted in a caveat. Pre-registered: unmeasured; the self tree's position-half claims may read violated on the handler-slice filename until its sanitisation is declared."  # fe98
    fields: {}  # fe98
